    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Troposphere height varies from approximately 8 km at the poles to 18 km at the equator.",
        "The Normal Lapse Rate in the Troposphere is a temperature decrease of 6.5°C per 1,000 meters of altitude.",
        "Commercial jet aircraft usually fly in the lower Stratosphere to avoid weather disturbances.",
        "Ionosphere contains electrically charged ions that reflect radio waves back to Earth, making wireless communication possible."
      ],
